│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zero_frontier_bias                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Bias simulated annealing proposals toward expanding the already-connected zero region. A  │
│                          │ valid zero region can generally only grow through its frontier, so uniformly selecting    │
│                          │ all 2500 cells wastes most iterations on proposals that immediately fail                  │
│                          │ zero-connectivity validation. The focused proposal selects a random zero cell and         │
│                          │ attempts to erase one of its nonzero grid neighbors. The remaining iterations retain the  │
│                          │ original unrestricted local recoloring proposal, preserving the ability to rearrange      │
│                          │ wards and escape local minima.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should substantially increase the number of meaningful positive-score proposals      │
│                          │ after the first zero tile has been created, while maintaining topology-changing           │
│                          │ exploration.                                                                              │
