│ patch_name               │ frontier_biased_sa                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Bias simulated annealing proposals toward expanding the existing zero region from its     │
│                          │ frontier. A valid new zero cell must remain connected to the outside-connected zero       │
│                          │ component, so uniformly selecting arbitrary cells wastes most attempts on impossible      │
│                          │ interior deletions. This change selects a random zero cell and a neighboring nonzero cell │
│                          │ with increasing probability as annealing progresses, while retaining random recoloring    │
│                          │ moves early in the search to escape local configurations. The result is substantially     │
│                          │ more useful validation attempts during the late optimization phase.                       │
