│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zero_frontier_bias                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Bias simulated-annealing proposals toward expanding the existing connected zero region.   │
│                          │ The current uniform-cell proposal spends most iterations on impossible conversions:       │
│                          │ changing a non-boundary, non-zero-frontier ward cell to zero immediately violates zero    │
│                          │ connectivity. Sampling a zero cell and one of its non-zero neighbors directly generates   │
│                          │ valid-connectivity candidates much more often, allowing substantially more useful         │
│                          │ removals within the same time budget.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fallback preserves the original proposal distribution, including recoloring moves     │
│                          │ that can restructure ward boundaries and occasional zero contractions required to escape  │
│                          │ local optima.                                                                             │
