│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zero_frontier_sampling                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Bias simulated annealing proposals toward expanding the already outside-connected zero    │
│                          │ region. A random deletion attempt has a low probability of being adjacent to color 0 and  │
│                          │ therefore usually fails the zero-connectivity check. Instead, selecting a random zero     │
│                          │ cell and one of its neighbors directly targets the zero frontier, where converting a      │
│                          │ neighboring ward cell to zero is structurally valid with respect to zero connectivity and │
│                          │ is much more likely to increase the score.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A minority of the original generic local proposals is retained so that the annealing      │
│                          │ phase can still recolor zero cells and reshape wards when necessary to preserve or create │
│                          │ required adjacencies.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
