│ patch_name               │ fast_erosion_sa                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the stronger one-pass greedy erosion schedule from the current       │
│                          │ program while incorporating a lower-overhead internal representation. The grid, color     │
│                          │ cell lists, BFS queue, adjacency counts, and temporary edge deltas are stored in          │
│                          │ fixed-size arrays instead of maps, nested vectors, and queue containers.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key improvements:                                                                         │
│                          │ - Replaces `std::map` temporary adjacency deltas with a tiny fixed array of at most eight │
│                          │ changed color pairs.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Uses flat arrays for the grid and color membership bookkeeping.                         │
│                          │ - Uses an array-based BFS queue.                                                          │
│                          │ - Avoids redundant connectivity checking for the newly assigned nonzero color: all        │
│                          │ nonzero proposals are copied from an adjacent cell, so that color remains connected by    │
│                          │ construction.                                                                             │
│                          │ - Recomputes SA temperature periodically rather than using `pow` every iteration.         │
│                          │ - Retains exact adjacency, ward connectivity, and outside-zero connectivity validation.   │
