│ patch_description        │ This redesign replaces nested vectors, maps, and queue objects with a flat-grid solver    │
│                          │ architecture. It uses fixed-size adjacency counters, compact per-color cell pools,        │
│                          │ transactional recoloring with a small fixed delta buffer, and array-based BFS             │
│                          │ connectivity checks. The search is organized into two phases: repeated randomized erosion │
│                          │ passes that aggressively grow the outside region, followed by simulated annealing         │
│                          │ neighborhood recoloring to escape local minima. This reduces allocation and map overhead  │
│                          │ while making rollback and validation substantially cheaper.                               │
