│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ frontier_peeling                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces expensive full-region validation and simulated annealing     │
│                          │ with a monotone frontier-peeling search.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It grows color `0` only from the outside-connected frontier, so zero-connectivity is      │
│                          │ guaranteed structurally. For each attempted removal or recoloring, it incrementally       │
│                          │ updates only the affected adjacency-pair counts. Connectivity of the removed ward is      │
│                          │ checked using a small articulation-style BFS between the same-colored neighbors of the    │
│                          │ changed cell, instead of BFS-checking both entire affected regions.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The solver repeatedly:                                                                    │
│                          │ - selects cells adjacent to outside/zero,                                                 │
│                          │ - tries to erase them into color `0`,                                                     │
│                          │ - occasionally performs local nonzero recoloring moves to reshape bottlenecks,            │
│                          │ - retains the best valid grid found.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This permits substantially more candidate evaluations within the time limit than the      │
│                          │ prior full connectivity-check approach.                                                   │
