│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_move_classes                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed 55%-to-zero proposal bias with three explicitly represented move        │
│                          │ classes: deletion (`nonzero -> 0`), restoration (`0 -> neighboring nonzero`), and nonzero │
│                          │ recoloring. The selection retains substantial base probability for every class, while     │
│                          │ periodically giving a modest bonus to classes whose recently proposed moves pass the      │
│                          │ strict topology/adjacency validator more often.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is intended to preserve the stronger broad random-neighbor exploration of the better │
│                          │ prior program, while avoiding spending most attempts on direct zero proposals when the    │
│                          │ current state has few deletable cells. Restoration remains available to rearrange         │
│                          │ bottlenecks, and nonzero recolors can change ward geometry without immediately            │
│                          │ sacrificing score.                                                                        │
