│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ best_restart_reheat                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add periodic restart-from-best diversification to the annealing phase. The current        │
│                          │ annealing state can drift below the saved best map after accepted negative moves and then │
│                          │ spend a large portion of the time budget exploring an inferior region. Rebuilding all     │
│                          │ mutable data structures after restoring `best_grid_state` is inexpensive on this fixed    │
│                          │ 50x50 board and guarantees consistency.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ After a sufficiently long stagnation period, restore the best legal state and temporarily │
│                          │ reheat the acceptance temperature. This preserves the strong incumbent while allowing     │
│                          │ several alternative reversible boundary changes to be explored from it, rather than       │
│                          │ continuing from a poor trajectory. The restart is disabled near the end so that the final │
│                          │ phase remains a low-temperature improvement search.                                       │
