│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ frontier_erosion                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the expensive full-region BFS validation and simulated       │
│                          │ annealing loop with a topology-aware randomized erosion method.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key observation is that every accepted state preserves connectivity. Therefore, when  │
│                          │ removing one cell from a color, it is sufficient to test whether that cell's same-colored │
│                          │ neighbors remain connected to each other; a full scan of the entire ward is unnecessary.  │
│                          │ Likewise, zero cells are only introduced from the exterior-connected zero component, so   │
│                          │ zero connectivity is maintained inductively.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm performs many randomized restarts. Within each restart it repeatedly:       │
│                          │ - tries to convert frontier cells into exterior-connected color `0`,                      │
│                          │ - preserves every required adjacency and forbids every non-required adjacency,            │
│                          │ - checks only local articulation behavior for the color losing a cell,                    │
│                          │ - occasionally performs connectivity-safe nonzero recoloring moves to reshape wards and   │
│                          │ unlock future erosion opportunities.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This uses local edge-count maintenance and local connectivity checks instead of global    │
│                          │ connectivity BFS after every move.                                                        │
