│ patch_description        │ Replace the single shuffled greedy pass with repeated randomized erosion passes that stop │
│                          │ when deletions have become unproductive. A cell that was not removable early in a pass    │
│                          │ may become removable after nearby cells are deleted, so revisiting cells can improve the  │
│                          │ initial zero region substantially. Conversely, several consecutive zero-yield blocks      │
│                          │ indicate that greedy erosion is exhausted; stopping then preserves the remaining budget   │
│                          │ for simulated annealing, where non-monotone restructuring is more valuable.               │
